From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:43:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/h264: do not parse ahead a subset SPS that replaces
 one in use

decode_nal_units() parses the subset SPSs of a packet before its other
NAL units, so that the views are known when the first slice of the base
view is decoded although the subset SPS comes later in the access unit
(the ones in mp4 and Matroska do that). It did so too for a subset SPS
that takes the place of one that declares views already. A packet can
begin with the dependent view of the access unit before it (the layout
of some Matroska files, which ff_h264_resolve_view_pair() deals with),
and where that unit is the last of a coded video sequence, its slices
were decoded against the subset SPS of the next sequence: with that
sequence's scaling matrices since fix 9006, which reads the PPS of a
dependent view against the subset SPS that the view activates.

Such a subset SPS is now parsed in NAL order. One whose id has no
subset SPS that declares views yet is parsed ahead as before: that is
what makes the views known. get_last_needed_nal() takes a packet that
holds a subset SPS of the first kind for one in which the views may be
decided again, and waits for its dependent view (fix 9005).

Measured with the stream made for fix 9006 from MVCSPS-1 of the ITU-T
H.264.1 conformance set (the stream twice, its subset SPS without a
matrix in the first copy, the PPSs not sent again in the second),
handed to the decoder packet by packet, one access unit a packet and in
that layout. Without this change the last picture of the second view
of the first copy differed between the two layouts, with one thread, 8
frame threads and 8 slice threads; with it the two layouts give the
same pictures. A stream that sends the same subset SPS again at each
sequence, or that brings a subset SPS with a new id, is decoded as
before.
---
diff --git a/libavcodec/h264dec.c b/libavcodec/h264dec.c
--- a/libavcodec/h264dec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/h264dec.c
@@ -547,6 +547,23 @@ static av_cold void h264_decode_flush(AVCodecContext *avctx)
         FF_HW_SIMPLE_CALL(avctx, flush);
 }
 
+/**
+ * Whether the subset SPS of this NAL unit has the id of one that declares views
+ * already. Only its id is read.
+ */
+static int subset_sps_replaces_views(const H264Context *h, const H2645NAL *nal)
+{
+    GetBitContext gb = nal->gb;
+    unsigned id;
+
+    if (get_bits_left(&gb) < 25)
+        return 0;
+    skip_bits(&gb, 24);             // profile_idc, the constraint flags, level_idc
+    id = get_ue_golomb_31(&gb);
+    return id < MAX_SPS_COUNT && h->ps.subset_sps_list[id] &&
+           h->ps.subset_sps_list[id]->mvc.num_views > 1;
+}
+
 /**
  * Whether the views are decided again while this packet is decoded, and a
  * dependent view can be turned on by it. h264_init_ps() does that at the first
@@ -557,6 +574,9 @@ static av_cold void h264_decode_flush(AVCodecContext *avctx)
  * choose cannot be known here.
  *
  * The subset SPS is found as h264_init_ps() finds it, by ff_h264_views_sps().
+ * A subset SPS of the packet that takes the place of one that declares views
+ * is not parsed before the packet is decoded (decode_nal_units()), and may come
+ * before that slice: the views may be decided again then.
  */
 static int dependent_view_may_start(const H264Context *h)
 {
@@ -565,6 +585,11 @@ static int dependent_view_may_start(const H264Context *h)
     if (h->views_active_decode != 1 || h->avctx->hwaccel)
         return 0;
 
+    for (int i = 0; i < h->pkt.nb_nals; i++)
+        if (h->pkt.nals[i].type == H264_NAL_SUB_SPS &&
+            subset_sps_replaces_views(h, &h->pkt.nals[i]))
+            return 1;
+
     sps = ff_h264_views_sps(h);
     return sps && sps != h->mvc_sps;
 }
@@ -710,11 +735,17 @@ static int decode_nal_units(H264Context *h, AVBufferRef *buf_ref,
      * the dependent view slices of the access unit it belongs to, and the ones in
      * mp4 and Matroska do exactly that. Picking it up in NAL order would leave
      * the views unknown while the first access unit is decoded, and its dependent
-     * slices would be dropped below. Parse them all up front instead: subset SPSs
+     * slices would be dropped below. Parse them up front instead: subset SPSs
      * have their own id space (ps.subset_sps_list) and cannot affect the base
-     * view, so hoisting them changes nothing else. */
+     * view.
+     * Not one that takes the place of a subset SPS that declares views already:
+     * the views are known then, and a packet can begin with the dependent view
+     * of the access unit before (the layout that some Matroska files have, see
+     * ff_h264_resolve_view_pair()), which belongs to the coded video sequence of
+     * the subset SPS being replaced. That one is parsed in NAL order. */
     for (i = 0; i < h->pkt.nb_nals; i++)
-        if (h->pkt.nals[i].type == H264_NAL_SUB_SPS) {
+        if (h->pkt.nals[i].type == H264_NAL_SUB_SPS &&
+            !subset_sps_replaces_views(h, &h->pkt.nals[i])) {
             /* on a copy: the NAL is parsed again in NAL order below */
             GetBitContext tmp_gb = h->pkt.nals[i].gb;
             ff_h264_decode_subset_seq_parameter_set(&tmp_gb, avctx, &h->ps);
